Yes, you can use C# code to determine the non-linear equation that best models the relationship between two variables X and Y in a SQL database table. One way to do this is to use specialized regression functions such as NLREG or NLS.
Here is an example code using the NLREG function:
```csharp
using System;
using NLREG;
namespace NonlinearRegression
{
    class Program
    {
        static void Main(string[] args)
        {
            // Load data from SQL database table
            double[] xData = { 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 };
            double[] yData = { 2.1, 4.0, 6.1, 7.9, 10.2 };
            // Define the non-linear equation to be fitted
            string equation = "A + B * Exp(-C * X)";
            // Set initial parameter estimates
            double[] parameters = { 10, 1, 0.1 };
            // Fit the non-linear equation to the data
            NLREG nlreg = new NLREG();
            nlreg.SetInputXYData(xData, yData);
            nlreg.SetNLFunction(equation);
            nlreg.SetInitParamValues(parameters);
            nlreg.Fit();
            // Get the optimized parameter values
            double[] optimizedParams = nlreg.GetOptimizedParamValues();
            // Print the optimized parameter values
            Console.WriteLine("Optimized parameter values:");
            Console.WriteLine("A = " + optimizedParams[0]);
            Console.WriteLine("B = " + optimizedParams[1]);
            Console.WriteLine("C = " + optimizedParams[2]);
            // Use the optimized equation to predict Y for a given value of X
            double x = 6;
            double yPredicted = optimizedParams[0] + optimizedParams[1] * Math.Exp(-optimizedParams[2] * x);
            Console.WriteLine("Predicted Y for X = " + x + " is " + yPredicted);
            // Identify outliers in the data
            double[] residuals = nlreg.GetResiduals();
            double[] stdErrors = nlreg.GetStdErrors();
            for (int i = 0; i < residuals.Length; i++)
            {
                if (Math.Abs(residuals[i]) > 2 * stdErrors[i])
                {
                    Console.WriteLine("Outlier detected at index " + i);
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
```
In this example, we load data from a SQL database table and define a non-linear equation to be fitted using the NLREG function. We set initial parameter estimates and fit the equation to the data. We then get the optimized parameter values and use them to predict Y for a given value of X. Finally, we identify outliers in the data by comparing the residuals to the standard errors.

