Yes, we can definitely utilize advanced letter frequency analysis and common word patterns to improve our accuracy in guessing letters in Hangman. We can also implement a more sophisticated approach for guessing the word based on partial knowledge of its length and common letter combinations.
Here is an implementation of a Hangman guessing algorithm in MATLAB that incorporates these techniques:
```matlab
function [guess, letters] = hangman(words, guessed_letters)
% words is a cell array of possible words
% guessed_letters is a string of all guessed letters so far
% Initialize letter frequency count
freq = zeros(1, 26);
% Update frequency count based on guessed letters
for i = 1:length(guessed_letters)
    letter = guessed_letters(i);
    if letter >= 'a' && letter <= 'z'
        freq(letter - 'a' + 1) = freq(letter - 'a' + 1) + 1;
    end
end
% Find the most common letter
[~, idx] = max(freq);
guess = char('a' + idx - 1);
% Update list of guessed letters
letters = [guessed_letters, guess];
% Find words that match the pattern (e.g. '_a__a_')
pattern = '';
for i = 1:length(guessed_letters)
    letter = guessed_letters(i);
    if letter >= 'a' && letter <= 'z'
        pattern = [pattern, letter];
    end
    if letter == '_'
        pattern = [pattern, '.'];
    end
end
matches = regexp(words, pattern);
% Find the most common word
word_freq = zeros(1, length(words));
for i = 1:length(matches)
    if ~isempty(matches{i})
        word = matches{i};
        for j = 1:length(word)
            letter = word(j);
            if letter >= 'a' && letter <= 'z'
                word_freq(i) = word_freq(i) + freq(letter - 'a' + 1);
            end
        end
    end
end
[~, idx] = max(word_freq);
guess_word = words{idx};
% Return the most common letter and word
guess = guess_word(1);
end
```
This algorithm first calculates the frequency of each letter based on the guessed letters so far. It then guesses the most common letter and updates the list of guessed letters. 
Next, it constructs a pattern based on the guessed letters and uses regular expressions to find all words that match that pattern. It then calculates a frequency score for each word based on the frequency of its letters and the frequency of the guessed letters. Finally, it returns the word with the highest frequency score as the guess.
This algorithm should be fairly efficient and accurate in guessing letters and words in Hangman.

